          "verdict_mentions": [
            "BLOCK"
          ],
          "opening_lines": [
            "# BLOCK \u2014 organization OIDC SSO and group sharing",
            "",
            "Reviewed on 2026-10-11. This verdict applies to `871cdf86942da2af17688a1be8427db34c77a027`, compared with baseline `7f5d619`. The current head must not ship: an unauthenticated client can exhaust login capacity across organizations, and ID-token validation accepts an untrusted additional audience. The redirect and provider-discovery findings below also require fixes. Approval requires verification of those fixes, a green full suite and race gate, and the real-tenant acceptance already required by the implementation's setup guide.",
            "",
            "The account and group isolation design held up in the local attacks. No cross-org authorization bypass or configuration takeover was demonstrated. The findings are specific failures with reproducible evidence, rather than a rejection of the overall subject-isolation design.",
            "",
            "## Scope and source integrity",
            "",
            "Read the review `BRIEF.md` in full, `/work/lanes/tunn-sso/final.md`, and the repository's complete `DESIGN.md` and `ENTERPRISE-ZT.md`. The two design documents are in `tunn/`, rather than alongside `final.md`. Reviewed the setup/validation documents and the changes in all three commits:",
            "",
            "- `f028f1f8dc44540da9e50cc9587c7904b6966568`: scoped design and enterprise roadmap.",
            "- `1660f85fd3cd75f8799ef43fd6cbb13de9506a5e`: organization OIDC, provider group resolution, sessions and sharing integration."
          ]
        }
      ],
