          "opening_lines": [
            "# Native OpenSSH jump host \u2014 security review round 2",
            "",
            "**Verdict: SHIP-AFTER-FIXES.** All six round-one fixes passed independent checks, including the original reproductions and adjacent variants. Before Internet-facing deployment, upgrade the inherited gRPC and QUIC dependencies and resolve the intermittent head-only race-suite assertion described below. This is not an unconditional deployment approval.",
            "",
            "Reviewed on 2026-10-11: head `2325a0f1b277a1ee8ecfc21cc73d17b09e1b17ff`, containing native jump commit `c2a252c179bed4838cf23cda429ff8c5fe6080f1`; comparison base `4b7364503e428837b6fdb98e8c2ce4605b05da90`. The reviewed repository was used only for reads. Git archives, tests, builds, dependency caches, temporary files and this report are under `/work/lanes/tunn-sshj/review2`. No production system, external recipient or deployment was involved.",
            "",
            "## Deployment findings",
            "",
            "### R2-F1 \u2014 High: inherited gRPC allocation DoS remains reachable",
            "",
            "The selected and built dependency is `google.golang.org/grpc v1.76.0`. [GO-2026-6348](https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/security/advisories/GHSA-vp52-pcj8-j9qc) describes excessive allocation from fragmented HTTP/2 DATA, fixed in v1.83.1. Public requests reach `createHTTP2Router` \u2192 `grpc.Server.ServeHTTP` at [proxy.go](/work/lanes/tunn-sshj/tunn/internal/host/proxy.go:804). `EstablishTunnel` reads the first registration message before authenticating its contents at [grpc_server.go](/work/lanes/tunn-sshj/tunn/internal/host/grpc_server.go:207).",
            ""
          ]
        }
      ],
